G4912.b:
⟪συν-έχω⟫
[in LXX for ⁨עצר⁩, ⁨חבר⁩, etc. ;]
⟪1.⟫ ⟪to hold together⟫ (τ. συνέχον τ. πάντα, Wi 1:7): of closing the ears, ⟦Acts 7:57|Ac 7:57⟧ (τ. στόμα, ⟦Isaiah 52:15|Is 52:15⟧); ⟪to hem in, press on every side⟫: ⟦Luke 8:45|Lk 8:45⟧ ⟦Luke 19:43|19:43⟧.
⟪2.⟫ ⟪to hold fast⟫;
⟪(a)⟫ of a prisoner, ⟪to hold in charge⟫ (Luc.; cf. exx. in Deiss., BS, 160; MM, xxiv): ⟦Luke 22:63|Lk 22:63⟧;
⟪(b)⟫ ⟪to constrain⟫: ⟦2 Corinthians 5:14|II Co 5:14⟧; pass., ⟦Luke 12:50|Lk 12:50⟧, ⟦Acts 18:5|Ac 18:5⟧ (τ. λόγῳ; cf. Field, Notes, 128), ⟦Philippians 1:23|Phl 1:23⟧; in pass., of ills, ⟪to be seized or afflicted by, suffering from⟫: ⟦Matthew 4:24|Mt 4:24⟧, ⟦Luke 4:38|Lk 4:38⟧ ⟦Luke 8:37|8:37⟧, ⟦Acts 28:8|Ac 28:8⟧.†

G4921.b:
⟪συν-ίστημι⟫
[in LXX for ⁨צוה⁩ pi., ⁨קהל⁩ ni., etc.; I Mac 12:43, II Mac 4:24, III Mac 1:19 (and freq. in these books) ;]
⟪1.⟫ trans.,
⟪(a)⟫ ⟪to commend, recommend⟫: c. acc. pers., ⟦2 Corinthians 3:1|II Co 3:1⟧ ⟦2 Corinthians 6:4|6:4⟧ ⟦2 Corinthians 10:12|10:12⟧, ⟦2 Corinthians 10:18|18⟧; id. c. dat., ⟦Romans 16:1|Ro 16:1⟧ (as freq. at the beginning of a letter; Deiss., LAE, 226), ⟦2 Corinthians 5:12|II Co 5:12⟧; seq. πρός, ⟦2 Corinthians 4:2|II Co 4:2⟧; pass., seq. ὑπό, ⟦2 Corinthians 12:11|II Co 12:11⟧;
⟪(b)⟫ ⟪to show, prove, establish⟫: c. acc., ⟦Romans 3:5|Ro 3:5⟧ ⟦Romans 5:8|5:8⟧, ⟦2 Corinthians 6:4|II Co 6:4⟧; dupl. acc., ⟦Galatians 2:13|Ga 2:13⟧; acc. et inf., ⟦2 Corinthians 7:11|II Co 7:11⟧
⟪2.⟫ Intrans., pf., συνέστηκα (as also 2 aor. and plpf.);
⟪(a)⟫ ⟪to stand with or near⟫: ⟦Luke 9:32|Lk 9:32⟧;
⟪(b)⟫ ⟪to be composed of, consist, cohere⟫: ⟦Colossians 1:17|Col 1:17⟧ (v. Lft., in l.), ⟦2 Peter 3:5|II Pe 3:5⟧.†

G4966.b:
⟪Συχέμ⟫ indecl. (Heb. ⁨שְׁכֶם⁩), ⟪Shechem⟫;
⟪1.⟫ the son of Hamor (⟦Genesis 33:19|Ge 33:19⟧): ⟦Acts 7:16|Ac 7:16 b⟧, Rec.
⟪2.⟫ A city of Samaria (AV, Sychem; in LXX also sometimes Σίκιμα, -ων, as in FlJ): ⟦Acts 7:16|Ac 7:16 a,b⟧.†

G4972.b:
⟪σφραγίζω⟫
[in LXX chiefly for ⁨חתם⁩ (⟦Deuteronomy 32:34|De 32:34⟧, al.), also for ⁨סתם⁩ (⟦Daniel 8:26|Da TH 8:26⟧) ;] ⟪to seal⟫,
⟪(a)⟫ for security: ⟦Matthew 27:66|Mt 27:66⟧, ⟦Revelation 20:3|Re 20:3⟧; τ. καρπὸν τοῦτον, fig. (cf. Deiss., BS, 238 f.; MM, xxiv; DB, iv, 427a), ⟦Romans 15:28|Ro 15:28⟧;
⟪(b)⟫ for concealment, hence, metaph., ⟪to hide⟫ (⟦Daniel 9:24|Da TH 9:24⟧, ⟦John 14:17|Jo 14:17⟧): ⟦Revelation 10:4|Re 10:4⟧ ⟦Revelation 22:10|22:10⟧;
⟪(c)⟫ for distinction, ⟦Revelation 7:3|Re 7:3-8⟧; metaph., ⟦Ephesians 1:13|Eph 1:13⟧ ⟦Ephesians 4:30|4:30⟧; mid., ⟦2 Corinthians 1:22|II Co 1:22⟧;
⟪(d)⟫ for authentication (⟦Ezra 8:8|Es 8:8⟧): ⟦John 3:33|Jo 3:33⟧ ⟦John 6:27|6:27⟧ (cf. κατα-σφραγίζω).†

G4988.b:
⟪Σωσθένης⟫, -ου, ὁ ⟪Sosthenes⟫;
⟪(a)⟫ a Jewish ruler: ⟦Acts 18:7|Ac 18:7⟧;
⟪(b)⟫ a Christian: ⟦1 Corinthians 1:1|I Co 1:1⟧.†
